---
import UseCaseLayout from '../../layouts/UseCaseLayout.astro';
import { productCopy } from '../../components/product-copy';
---
<UseCaseLayout
  title="Replaid for Automation Agencies | Connect Your Clients’ Agents"
  description="Connect the AI agents you build to your clients’ customer conversations. Use Replaid for channel connections, reply permissions, and action records."
  audience="For automation agencies"
  source="agencies"
  intro="Build the assistant your client needs. Use Replaid to connect it to customer messages, control its actions, and review what happened."
>
  <Fragment slot="heading">Your agent. Your client. <span class="hero-highlight">Their conversations, connected.</span></Fragment>
  <aside slot="example" class="use-case-example" aria-label="Example client workflow">
    <p class="example-label">Example client workflow</p>
    <div class="example-message"><span>A customer asks on Instagram</span><p>“Do you deliver on Saturdays?”</p></div>
    <dl class="example-steps">
      <div><dt>Your agent</dt><dd>Reads the delivery policy you prepared with the client.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Replaid</dt><dd>Checks permissions and saves the proposed reply.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Your client</dt><dd>Reviews the draft before sending is enabled.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="example-result">First test: draft only. No customer reply is sent.</p>
  </aside>

  <section class="use-case-section" aria-labelledby="agency-delivery-heading">
    <header><h2 id="agency-delivery-heading">A clear place for each part of the work.</h2><p>Keep control of the agent you deliver and the service you provide.</p></header>
    <div class="use-case-columns">
      <article><h3>You build the agent</h3><p>Choose the agent, prepare the business knowledge, and define reply instructions and triggers. Keep the client relationship and ongoing service with your agency.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Your client connects their channels</h3><p>An authorized account owner completes the channel connection. Agree on what the agent can read, draft, and send before the first test.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Replaid carries out allowed actions</h3><p>Give the agent access to conversations through MCP or REST. Review recorded actions and pause automation when a conversation needs a person.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="use-case-section use-case-split" aria-labelledby="agency-start-heading">
    <header><h2 id="agency-start-heading">Start with one client and one workflow.</h2><p>Make the first installation easy to check before you expand its scope.</p><p>Choosing a platform for a client? <a class="use-case-link" href="/compare/manychat/">Compare Replaid and Manychat</a> before you plan the workflow.</p></header>
    <ol class="use-case-checklist">
      <li><h3>Choose the questions to handle</h3><p>For example, common delivery questions. Collect the facts the agent needs and define when it must ask a person.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Test with sending disabled</h3><p>Connect one channel. Ask the agent to read a test conversation and prepare a draft. Review the answer with the client.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Agree on operation and maintenance</h3><p>Decide how the agent starts, who reviews failures, and which changes your service includes. Enable sending only for the agreed scope.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="use-case-section use-case-questions" aria-labelledby="agency-questions-heading">
    <h2 id="agency-questions-heading">Before you offer it to a client.</h2>
    <div class="sky-faq-list">
      <details class="sky-faq-item"><summary>Does Replaid build or run the agent for my agency?</summary><p>No. You provide the agent, knowledge, instructions, and the way it starts. Replaid connects it to conversations and carries out permitted actions. Optional setup help is a separate paid service.</p></details>
      <details class="sky-faq-item"><summary>What should I allow for in the client quote?</summary><p>Your setup and maintenance work, Replaid access per team, any paid channel usage, and your external agent or AI provider costs. <a href="/pricing/">Review pricing and included access.</a></p></details>
      <details class="sky-faq-item"><summary>Which account limits should I check?</summary><p>{productCopy.channelLimits} <a href="/docs/connect-your-agent/#channel">Check the requirements for your client’s channel.</a></p></details>
    </div>
  </section>
</UseCaseLayout>
